      "message": "\u003e This does not convey the semantics properly. Since all library types will share the same prefix, I suggest (underscore prefixing to denote a private variable):\n\u003e \n\u003e   set(_lib_prefix \"lib\")\n\u003e   set(CMAKE_SHARED_LIBRARY_PREFIX \"${_lib_prefix}\")\n\u003e   set(CMAKE_IMPORT_LIBRARY_PREFIX \"${_lib_prefix}\")\n\u003e   set(CMAKE_STATIC_LIBRARY_PREFIX \"${_lib_prefix}\")\n\u003e   \n\u003e Adjust the underscore in the remaining instances as appropriate.\n\nGood point, though cmake reserves _ names in some cases [1]. We have existing pkg-config related variable above, so I\u0027ll stick with this name for now.\n\n[1] https://cmake.org/cmake/help/latest/manual/cmake-language.7.html#variables",
